WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.540
Hey, welcome back.

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.660
Connect a resistor, inductor and capacitor in series to a sinusoidal source.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.530
There is only one series current, but the three element voltages do not peak

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:11.640
at

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.280
the same time.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.720
That is why adding their magnitudes as ordinary positive numbers gives the

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:17.740
wrong source voltage.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.360
Use current as our phasor reference.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.780
Resistor voltage points along current.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.720
Inductor voltage leads it by ninety degrees, so draw it upward.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.920
Capacitor voltage lags by ninety degrees, so draw it downward.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.180
The inductive and capacitive voltage phasors oppose each other.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.580
Their net vertical contribution is current times X L minus X C.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.100
The horizontal contribution is current times R.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.420
The source voltage is the vector sum.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.720
Here, all phasor lengths represent RMS magnitudes; peak values would also work

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:52.740
if used consistently.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:59.740
Suppose RMS current is two amperes, R is thirty ohms, X L is

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.840
seventy ohms and X C is thirty ohms.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.080
Resistor voltage is sixty volts.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.838
Inductor voltage is one hundred forty volts, capacitor voltage sixty volts,

00:01:07.838 --> 00:01:08.000
and

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.360
their difference eighty volts.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:13.680
The source magnitude is the square root of sixty squared plus eighty squared:

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.960
one hundred volts.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.220
It is not two hundred sixty volts.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.840
Phasors encode time relationships; they are not literal spatial voltage arrows

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:22.368
inside the wires.

00:01:22.368 --> 00:01:28.148
Factor current out of the phasor triangle and you get impedance Z: square root

00:01:28.148 --> 00:01:32.928
of R squared plus the square of X L minus X C.

00:01:32.928 --> 00:01:37.408
Impedance has units ohms, but includes timing effects as well as resistance.

00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:41.868
RMS current equals RMS source voltage divided by Z.

00:01:42.608 --> 00:01:46.668
The phase angle phi is source voltage phase minus current phase, and its

00:01:46.668 --> 00:01:50.168
tangent is X L minus X C divided by R.

00:01:50.488 --> 00:01:55.748
With R thirty ohms and net reactance forty ohms, impedance is fifty ohms.

00:01:56.648 --> 00:01:59.868
A one hundred volt RMS source gives two amperes RMS.

00:02:00.788 --> 00:02:03.248
The phase angle is about fifty three point one degrees.

00:02:04.128 --> 00:02:08.468
Because net reactance is positive, source voltage leads current, or current

00:02:08.468 --> 00:02:08.988
lags.

00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:14.328
Now swap the reactances: X L thirty ohms and X C seventy ohms.

00:02:15.408 --> 00:02:20.008
Impedance still equals fifty ohms and current magnitude stays two amperes, but

00:02:20.008 --> 00:02:21.008
phi is negative.

00:02:21.888 --> 00:02:24.988
Current now leads the source voltage by the same angle magnitude.

00:02:26.148 --> 00:02:28.388
Magnitude alone cannot tell you the lead or lag.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.888
The sign of net reactance matters.

00:02:31.708 --> 00:02:36.808
Our formula assumes a series circuit, ideal L and C, positive total resistance

00:02:37.208 --> 00:02:38.508
and sinusoidal steady state.

00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:43.568
Do not reuse it unchanged for a parallel circuit, and do not mix RMS source

00:02:43.568 --> 00:02:46.468
voltage with peak current when calculating impedance.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.180
Resonance occurs when inductive and capacitive reactances match.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:53.380
Set omega L equal to one over omega C.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:59.380
Rearranging gives resonance angular frequency one over square root of L C.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:03.480
Ordinary resonance frequency is that angular frequency divided by two pi.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:09.130
At resonance, net reactance is zero, impedance equals resistance and current

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:09.260
is

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.620
in phase with the source voltage.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.260
For a fixed source amplitude and constant total resistance, the series current

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:16.440
reaches its maximum.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.820
Try L equal to zero point one henry and C equal to one hundred microfarads.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.180
Their product is ten to the minus five, giving angular frequency about three

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.541
hundred sixteen point two radians per second and ordinary frequency about

00:03:30.541 --> 00:03:30.840
fifty

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:31.540
point three hertz.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:37.260
With RMS source voltage one hundred volts and R twenty ohms, resonance current

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.860
is five amperes RMS.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.840
Do the inductor and capacitor voltages vanish?

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.380
Pause before answering.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:44.500
No.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:49.180
Each reactance is about thirty one point six ohms, so each element voltage is

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.120
about one hundred fifty eight volts RMS.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.820
Their phasors cancel each other in the source sum.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:58.280
An element voltage can exceed the source voltage without violating energy

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:58.800
conservation.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:02.000
Our finite resistance model keeps current finite.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:07.334
The ideal zero resistance driven resonant system needs a transient analysis;

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:07.460
do

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.220
not promise an ordinary finite steady state current there.

00:04:10.392 --> 00:04:15.572
The source voltage and current may be out of phase, so multiplying their RMS

00:04:15.572 --> 00:04:18.932
magnitudes does not always give average transferred power.

00:04:19.852 --> 00:04:24.772
The correct expression is RMS voltage times RMS current times cosine phi.

00:04:25.612 --> 00:04:27.372
That cosine is the power factor.

00:04:28.112 --> 00:04:30.692
In our series model it equals R over Z.

00:04:31.812 --> 00:04:36.352
For the thirty ohm resistor and fifty ohm impedance example, power factor is

00:04:36.352 --> 00:04:37.332
zero point six.

00:04:38.212 --> 00:04:43.572
RMS voltage one hundred volts and RMS current two amperes give average power

00:04:43.572 --> 00:04:44.672
one hundred twenty watts.

00:04:45.972 --> 00:04:50.632
Check another way: current squared times resistance is four times thirty, also

00:04:50.632 --> 00:04:51.712
one hundred twenty watts.

00:04:52.752 --> 00:04:57.492
The product V RMS times I RMS is two hundred volt amperes of apparent power,

00:04:58.172 --> 00:05:00.532
not two hundred watts of real power in this example.

00:05:01.752 --> 00:05:06.112
Ideal inductors and capacitors store and return energy, giving zero average

00:05:06.112 --> 00:05:07.232
dissipation individually.

00:05:08.412 --> 00:05:11.632
Real components add losses, which belong in a more complete model.

00:05:12.752 --> 00:05:16.312
At series resonance, phi is zero and power factor is one.

00:05:17.172 --> 00:05:21.652
An ideal pure reactive circuit has zero average power despite nonzero voltage

00:05:21.652 --> 00:05:22.212
and current.

00:05:22.992 --> 00:05:25.892
That does not mean instantaneous power is always zero.

00:05:26.752 --> 00:05:28.292
Energy goes back and forth over the cycle.

00:05:28.852 --> 00:05:33.410
In JEE numericals, first establish whether the provided voltage and current

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:33.592
are

00:05:33.592 --> 00:05:37.132
peak or RMS, then check whether a power factor is needed.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:41.180
Let's combine the ideas in one frequency test.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:47.220
Keep L zero point one henry, C one hundred microfarads, R twenty ohms

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.040
and RMS source voltage one hundred volts.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:55.200
Set angular frequency to two hundred radians per second, below the resonance

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.140
value of about three hundred sixteen.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:00.020
Inductive reactance is twenty ohms.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:02.580
Capacitive reactance is fifty ohms.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:08.180
Net reactance is minus thirty ohms, so the circuit is capacitive and current

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.600
leads the voltage.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:13.400
Impedance is square root of twenty squared plus thirty squared, about thirty

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.720
six point one ohms.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.180
RMS current is about two point seven seven amperes.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:23.710
Power factor is twenty over thirty six point one, about zero point five five

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:24.160
five.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.540
Average power is about one hundred fifty four watts.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:31.720
At resonance the current would be five amperes and average power five hundred

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.000
watts for this same fixed source and resistor.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.630
Now raise angular frequency to five hundred.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.480
X L becomes fifty ohms and X C becomes twenty ohms.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:45.080
Net reactance is plus thirty ohms: current lags.

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:49.140
The impedance and current magnitude happen to match our lower frequency case,

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:50.500
but phase reverses.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:54.820
That matching is specific to these numbers, not a general equal spacing

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:55.640
frequency rule.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:00.700
Recalculate both reactances whenever frequency changes, then use their

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:02.780
difference, the impedance and the power factor.
